      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] A few improvements for the commit message:\n\n1. **Scope / Bundled changes**: The subject line joins two separate fixes with `\" and \"` (`Fix FIFO ODR on power-off and propagate error`), and the diff also includes an undocumented third change in `zephyr/emul/emul_lsm6dso.c` (decrementing the FIFO status sample count when reading `LSM6DSO_FIFO_DATA_ADDR_TAG`). Ideally, split this CL into focused CLs (see top-level review summary).\n2. **Avoid narrating code syntax**: Describe the behavior and cause in prose rather than quoting C expressions and compiler builtins (`data-\u003ebase.odr \u003d\u003d 0`, `__fls(0)`, `__builtin_clz(0)`, `accelgyro_config_fifo(s)`).\n3. **`TEST\u003d` target**: `-s drivers.default` only runs the default test suite and does not run the new `drivers.lsm6dso` test suite (`./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dso`).\n\nIf split as recommended, the commit message for the primary CL (power-off FIFO ODR fix) can be:\n\n```text\ndriver: accelgyro_lsm6dso: Disable FIFO ODR when sensor is powered off\n\nPassing a zero output data rate to the ODR-to-register conversion macro\ninvokes a find-last-set bit operation on zero, which is undefined\nbehavior and writes a non-zero batching rate into FIFO_CTRL3 when powering\noff a sensor. Explicitly write LSM6DSO_DIS_BIT when the configured ODR is\nzero so FIFO batching is disabled for powered-off sensors.\n\nBUG\u003db:441152198\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dso\n```\n\nOr if kept together with the error-propagation fix (after moving the unrelated emulator FIFO read decrement out):\n\n```text\ndriver: accelgyro_lsm6dso: Fix power-off FIFO ODR and error propagation\n\nPassing a zero output data rate to the ODR-to-register conversion macro\ninvokes a find-last-set bit operation on zero, which is undefined\nbehavior and writes a non-zero batching rate into FIFO_CTRL3 when powering\noff a sensor. Explicitly write LSM6DSO_DIS_BIT when the configured ODR is\nzero, and return any error from FIFO configuration when setting the sensor\ndata rate instead of discarding it.\n\nBUG\u003db:441152198\nTEST\u003d./twister -T zephyr/test/drivers -s drivers.lsm6dso\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/692e539d-70a2-4e12-81e8-26af5690dda6)",
