      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested** — Please address the inline issues (in particular, wiring `CONFIG_LINK_TEST_SUITE_LSM6DSO` into `Kconfig` and `testcase.yaml`, ensuring state transitions before assertions in the new tests, and splitting out the unrelated emulator FIFO read change).\n\n### Review Summary\n* **Functionality**: The fixes in `driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c` (`accelgyro_config_fifo()` using `LSM6DSO_DIS_BIT` when `data-\u003ebase.odr \u003d\u003d 0` instead of invoking `LSM6DSO_ODR_TO_REG(0)`, and `set_data_rate()` propagating the return value of `accelgyro_config_fifo(s)`) are sound. However, the new test suite in `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso` is never built or executed because `CONFIG_LINK_TEST_SUITE_LSM6DSO` is missing from `zephyr/test/drivers/Kconfig` and `drivers.lsm6dso` is missing from `zephyr/test/drivers/testcase.yaml`.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit**: The new test directory structure mirrors `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dsm`, and adding an emulator fault-injection helper in `zephyr/include/emul/emul_lsm6dso.h` fits the existing Zephyr driver test architecture.\n* **Code Simplicity**: Remove the unused `#include \u003czephyr/drivers/gpio.h\u003e` in `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c`.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability**:\n  * Replace the reserved double-underscore include guard `__EMUL_LSM6DSO_H` in `zephyr/include/emul/emul_lsm6dso.h` with `PLATFORM_EC_ZEPHYR_INCLUDE_EMUL_EMUL_LSM6DSO_H_`.\n  * Replace raw magic literals (`0x78` in `zephyr/emul/emul_lsm6dso.c`, `13000` and `0` in `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c`) with the existing named constants (`LSM6DSO_FIFO_DATA_ADDR_TAG`, `LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL`, `LSM6DSO_DIS_BIT`).\n* **Security**: N/A — No untrusted inputs, credentials, or sensitive data paths are modified.\n* **Testing**:\n  * Register `LINK_TEST_SUITE_LSM6DSO` in `zephyr/test/drivers/Kconfig` and `drivers.lsm6dso` in `zephyr/test/drivers/testcase.yaml`.\n  * In `test_accelgyro_config_fifo_power_off`, configure a non-zero ODR and verify non-zero `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL3_ADDR` bits before powering off, and test both `ACC_SENSOR_ID` and `GYR_SENSOR_ID` (`LSM6DSO_FIFO_ODR_MASK(s)` branches on sensor type).\n  * In `test_set_data_rate_fifo_error`, ensure `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL3_ADDR` starts from a different value (`0`) before calling `set_data_rate(acc, LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL, 1)` so `st_write_data_with_mask()` does not short-circuit on `new_data \u003d\u003d old_data`, and also cover `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL4_ADDR` write failure.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope**: `Size: M (+239, -2)`. This CL bundles three independent logical changes and should be split into focused CLs:\n  1. **CL 1 (`driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c`, `zephyr/test/drivers/CMakeLists.txt`, `zephyr/test/drivers/Kconfig`, `zephyr/test/drivers/testcase.yaml`, `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/*`)**: Fix `accelgyro_config_fifo()` to write `LSM6DSO_DIS_BIT` when `data-\u003ebase.odr \u003d\u003d 0` and add the `drivers.lsm6dso` unit test suite (`test_accelgyro_config_fifo_power_off`).\n  2. **CL 2 (`driver/accelgyro_lsm6dso.c`, `zephyr/emul/emul_lsm6dso.c`, `zephyr/include/emul/emul_lsm6dso.h`, `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c`)**: Propagate the return value of `accelgyro_config_fifo()` in `set_data_rate()`, add `lsm6dso_emul_set_write_fail_reg()`, and add `test_set_data_rate_fifo_error`.\n  3. **CL 3 (`zephyr/emul/emul_lsm6dso.c`, `zephyr/test/drivers/lsm6dso/src/main.c`)**: Decrement the unread FIFO sample count in `LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS1_ADDR`/`LSM6DSO_FIFO_STS2_ADDR` when reading `LSM6DSO_FIFO_DATA_ADDR_TAG` in `lsm6dso_emul_transfer_i2c()`, along with a unit test exercising FIFO reads.\n* **Commit Message**: See inline comment on `/COMMIT_MSG` to avoid joining independent actions with `\" and \"` in the subject, avoid narrating C expressions, and update `TEST\u003d` to `-s drivers.lsm6dso`.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/692e539d-70a2-4e12-81e8-26af5690dda6)",
