      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] In `test_set_data_rate_fifo_error`:\n\n1. **Short-circuit in `st_write_data_with_mask()`**: `st_write_data_with_mask()` reads `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL3_ADDR` first and returns `EC_SUCCESS` without calling `st_raw_write8()` if `new_data \u003d\u003d old_data`. In `sensor.dts`, `ec-s0` configures `10000 | ROUND_UP_FLAG`, which rounds up to `13000` mHz (`LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL`). If `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL3_ADDR` already holds the encoded value for `13000` mHz when this test starts, `set_data_rate(acc, 13000, 1)` will skip writing to `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL3_ADDR` and return `EC_SUCCESS` instead of triggering the injected failure. Ensure the sensor starts from a different ODR (e.g., `0`) before injecting the write failure.\n2. **Magic number**: Replace `13000` with `LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL`.\n3. **Additional FIFO config failure path**: `accelgyro_config_fifo()` also writes `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL4_ADDR` when disabling/enabling the FIFO mode; testing a write failure on `LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL4_ADDR` as well covers the remaining error returns in `accelgyro_config_fifo()`.\n\n```c\nZTEST(lsm6dso, test_set_data_rate_fifo_error)\n{\n\tconst struct emul *emul \u003d EMUL_DT_GET(LSM6DSO_NODE);\n\tstruct motion_sensor_t *acc \u003d \u0026motion_sensors[ACC_SENSOR_ID];\n\tint rv;\n\n\t/* Ensure FIFO_CTRL3 starts at 0 so setting LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL forces a write. */\n\trv \u003d acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_data_rate(acc, 0, 0);\n\tzassert_equal(rv, EC_SUCCESS);\n\n\tlsm6dso_emul_set_write_fail_reg(emul, LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL3_ADDR);\n\trv \u003d acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_data_rate(acc, LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL, 1);\n\tzassert_not_equal(rv, EC_SUCCESS);\n\n\tlsm6dso_emul_set_write_fail_reg(emul, LSM6DSO_FIFO_CTRL4_ADDR);\n\trv \u003d acc-\u003edrv-\u003eset_data_rate(acc, LSM6DSO_ODR_MIN_VAL, 1);\n\tzassert_not_equal(rv, EC_SUCCESS);\n\n\tlsm6dso_emul_set_write_fail_reg(emul, -1);\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/692e539d-70a2-4e12-81e8-26af5690dda6)",
